-- 20 original full-length IELTS-format tests, 40 questions each.
BEGIN;
CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lhbd_app;
SET LOCAL search_path TO lhbd_app;

DELETE FROM exams WHERE category IN ('Academic Practice Library','General Training Practice Library','Listening Practice Library');

DO $$
DECLARE eid integer; s1 integer; s2 integer; s3 integer;
BEGIN

Recently, planners have begun restoring wetlands rather than replacing them. Reeds and other aquatic plants slow the movement of water, while their roots create spaces in the soil where moisture can collect. These habitats also support birds and insects, giving residents contact with wildlife without leaving the city.

Restoration is not simply a matter of digging a pond. Engineers must understand where water enters and leaves the site, and local volunteers often help monitor plants and animals. Although some projects are expensive, researchers argue that avoided flood damage can make them economical over time.','Questions 1–13: Read or listen carefully and answer every question.','',1) RETURNING id INTO s1;

One area of interest is memory consolidation. After people practise a new skill, certain patterns of brain activity associated with that skill may reappear during sleep. This replay is thought to strengthen useful connections, making recall more reliable the following day. A single short night does not destroy memory, but repeated sleep loss can make learning less efficient.

Scientists also study how sleep affects attention. Even when tired people believe they are performing normally, brief lapses can occur without their awareness. For this reason, researchers recommend consistent sleep routines rather than relying on occasional long weekends to recover.','Questions 14–26: Read or listen carefully and answer every question.','',2) RETURNING id INTO s2;

Community repair cafés offer one response. Visitors bring broken objects and work alongside volunteers who share tools and practical knowledge. The aim is not only to fix an item but also to help owners understand how it works. Some cafés record the reasons for failure, providing useful information to manufacturers and campaigners.

New right-to-repair rules in several regions go further by requiring certain companies to supply parts and manuals. Critics worry about safety and intellectual property, while supporters argue that longer product lifetimes benefit both consumers and the environment.','Questions 27–40: Read or listen carefully and answer every question.','',3) RETURNING id INTO s3;
END $$;

