Bird counts are a familiar example. Thousands of participants record species on the same weekend, helping researchers identify changes in distribution over time. Similar projects monitor water quality, track insects and search astronomical photographs for unusual objects.

Large volunteer datasets still require careful checking. Organisers may ask experienced reviewers to inspect unusual records and provide feedback to contributors. When participants understand how their observations are used, they are more likely to remain involved and to improve the quality of future submissions.','Questions 27–40: Read or listen carefully and answer every question.','',3) RETURNING id INTO s3;
END $$;

