Drip irrigation is one widely used technique. Instead of spraying water across an entire field, pipes deliver small amounts close to plant roots. This can reduce evaporation, although blocked nozzles and poor maintenance may limit its effectiveness. The technology is most successful when farmers receive training and replacement parts are available locally.

Researchers also test crop varieties that tolerate heat and short dry periods. They caution that no single seed or device can solve every problem. Soil health, access to markets and fair water agreements all influence whether a farming community can remain resilient.','Questions 27–40: Read or listen carefully and answer every question.','',3) RETURNING id INTO s3;
END $$;

