Staff increasingly act as guides to digital information. A reader may ask for help evaluating a website, completing an official form or joining a video call. These services are particularly valuable where home internet is unreliable or devices are shared among family members.

Libraries must nevertheless make choices about limited budgets. Some reduce opening hours while others form partnerships with schools and community groups. Supporters argue that measuring success only by book loans misses the social and educational value of a free, welcoming public space.','Questions 27–40: Read or listen carefully and answer every question.','',3) RETURNING id INTO s3;
END $$;

